WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.179 --> 00:00:04.370
I mean… overall I’ve got to say that I
strongly dislike whenever you see a creator

00:00:04.370 --> 00:00:07.910
giving in to public outcry and changing their
artwork because of complainers.

00:00:07.910 --> 00:00:12.100
So… if you want to hear what my thoughts
are on this Happy Death Day controversy, then

00:00:12.100 --> 00:00:13.380
stick around to the end of this video.

00:00:17.590 --> 00:00:21.720
Welcome back to DeadTalks, the show where
I don’t release the episode a day early

00:00:21.730 --> 00:00:24.250
because we don’t want to mess with the YouTube
algorithm.

00:00:24.250 --> 00:00:28.110
So much of my job is just me trying appease
the mighty algorithm so that you people can

00:00:28.110 --> 00:00:29.620
actually see my videos.

00:00:29.620 --> 00:00:32.860
But Blumhouse is the company who made one
of the newer franchises in horror and it’s

00:00:32.860 --> 00:00:34.900
called Seven in Heaven.

00:00:36.040 --> 00:00:39.260
No, I’m kidding, but you already saw the
title, so you know that we’re talking about

00:00:39.260 --> 00:00:40.260
Happy Death Day.

00:00:40.260 --> 00:00:41.260
2U.

00:00:41.260 --> 00:00:44.670
And Happy Death Day 2U is getting a new release
date thanks to a tweet that reads:

00:00:44.670 --> 00:00:48.410
“My daughter and 16 others were killed on
February 14th.

00:00:48.410 --> 00:00:51.760
Universal Studios is releasing a move a movie
called Happy Death Day 2 U?

00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:56.530
I get the pun on Valentines Day, for me it
will always be the day my daughter was murdered.

00:00:56.530 --> 00:00:57.969
Please reconsider this!!!!”

00:00:57.969 --> 00:01:01.649
He is of course referring to the Florida school incident
that happened last year.

00:01:01.649 --> 00:01:04.070
Universal responded by issuing the following
statement.

00:01:04.070 --> 00:01:07.830
“When Universal Pictures became aware last
week that the one-year anniversary of the

00:01:07.830 --> 00:01:12.111
tragic events in Parkland, Florida fell on
the Happy Death Day 2U release date, the studio

00:01:12.111 --> 00:01:15.880
spoke with victim advocates and immediately
began the process of changing the release

00:01:15.880 --> 00:01:17.380
date of the film.”

00:01:17.380 --> 00:01:18.549
So they moved it up.

00:01:18.549 --> 00:01:20.360
To February 13.

00:01:20.360 --> 00:01:21.690
So what do I think about this.

00:01:21.690 --> 00:01:26.400
Well, if you came here to see me rip them
a new one for caving into to societal pressure,

00:01:26.400 --> 00:01:30.330
I guess you’re gonna be disappointed, because
this move seems more or less fine to me, but

00:01:30.330 --> 00:01:31.549
I do have some thoughts about it.

00:01:31.549 --> 00:01:36.120
The title is literally Happy Death Day, and
this day happens to be the one year anniversary…

00:01:36.120 --> 00:01:39.730
it sounds weird saying anniversary, cause
usually anniversary is like you’re celebrating

00:01:39.730 --> 00:01:40.730
something.

00:01:40.730 --> 00:01:44.320
But it is the one year mark of one of the
most prolific American tragedies of 2018,

00:01:44.320 --> 00:01:47.579
so just the title alone, I think it’s kind
of understandable just because it seems to

00:01:47.579 --> 00:01:49.659
be such a specific reference.

00:01:49.659 --> 00:01:51.770
And moving up the release date doesn’t really
hurt anything.

00:01:51.770 --> 00:01:54.580
If you were planning on seeing it on the 14th
you still can.

00:01:54.580 --> 00:01:58.220
If you’re a huge Happy Death Day fan and
you already pre-ordered for the 14th, I’m

00:01:58.220 --> 00:02:00.310
sure you can still get your ticket changed
if you want to.

00:02:00.310 --> 00:02:04.159
And it’s not like they changed the content
of the movie or worse, cancelled the movie;

00:02:04.159 --> 00:02:07.119
the artistic intention isn’t changed by
moving up the release date.

00:02:07.119 --> 00:02:10.659
Now I know there are some films that actually
do have creativity put into the release date,

00:02:10.659 --> 00:02:14.519
but it’s not like they’re moving a Star
Wars movie off of May the 4th or altering

00:02:14.519 --> 00:02:16.670
Don’t Hug Me I’m.Scared from a June 19th
release date.

00:02:16.670 --> 00:02:20.290
I mean, it’s February 14th, it’s clearly
just to try to cash on people going to the

00:02:20.290 --> 00:02:21.609
movies for Valentine’s.

00:02:21.609 --> 00:02:24.209
Moving the release date by one day seems like
a win for everyone.

00:02:24.209 --> 00:02:28.010
It appeases those affected by the shooting,
it doesn’t really affect the studio and

00:02:28.010 --> 00:02:32.120
even kind of makes them look like the good
guy, and fans can see it a day early or still

00:02:32.120 --> 00:02:33.930
see it on that day if they want.

00:02:33.930 --> 00:02:38.019
But there are people voicing their… uhh…
voices* about this.

00:02:38.019 --> 00:02:40.109
“I’m sorry, this is ridiculous.

00:02:40.109 --> 00:02:41.379
Tragedies happen every day.”

00:02:41.379 --> 00:02:44.319
But I feel like this is such a specific example
because of the title.

00:02:44.319 --> 00:02:47.519
If people were to go and start complaining
about other horror movies and other release

00:02:47.519 --> 00:02:51.659
dates, because x movie has blood and y tragedy
has blood, then I would say that we’ve crossed

00:02:51.659 --> 00:02:52.659
the line at that point.

00:02:52.659 --> 00:02:55.170
But for Happy Death Day, I’d say it’s
a good idea to move it.

00:02:55.170 --> 00:02:58.860
Now they also announced that they won’t
be marketing the movie in that area of Florida,

00:02:58.860 --> 00:03:02.239
which is fine, and they won’t be screening
it over there either, which kind of reminds

00:03:02.239 --> 00:03:06.450
me of how Sony didn’t show Slenderman in
parts of Minnesota because of the Slenderman

00:03:06.450 --> 00:03:08.150
stabbing that happened over there.

00:03:08.150 --> 00:03:12.310
Cancelling the screenings seems a little bit
like… maybe unfair to the fans who just

00:03:12.310 --> 00:03:15.499
innocently wanted to see the movie and now
they’ll have to travel to see it.

00:03:15.499 --> 00:03:19.129
I was thinking they should just let the movie
play, pull the marketing and it’s not like

00:03:19.129 --> 00:03:21.189
anyone would be forced to buy tickets.

00:03:21.189 --> 00:03:24.620
But then I think about the classmates going
to movies and just seeing that on the marquee.

00:03:24.620 --> 00:03:28.449
And it’s not as if people are going to see
Happy Death Day up on the marquee and burst

00:03:28.449 --> 00:03:29.449
into tears.

00:03:29.449 --> 00:03:30.449
It has been a full year.

00:03:30.449 --> 00:03:33.909
But I still do understand how it’s kind
of a class act for Universal to pull the film

00:03:33.909 --> 00:03:37.220
in that area, and it won’t be impossible
for the people who really want to see it to

00:03:37.220 --> 00:03:40.889
make the drive, so I really don’t think
it’s as big of a deal as some people, who

00:03:40.889 --> 00:03:43.930
I understand are probably the vocal minority,
are making it out to be.

00:03:43.930 --> 00:03:46.870
But be sure to let me know your thoughts on
this in the comments.

00:03:46.870 --> 00:03:50.650
Like I said, hopefully this is a one time
thing because it's so specific and it's not

00:03:50.650 --> 00:03:53.969
going to snowball into a situation where
all horror movies are banned on the day of

00:03:53.969 --> 00:03:57.739
every shooting, because the way things are
going, there aren’t gonna be a whole lot

00:03:57.739 --> 00:03:58.869
of days left.

00:03:58.869 --> 00:04:01.739
I'll see you in the next one.

